From: aegis-statefulset architecture team
Subject: [PATCH] Switch DR-tier Schedule B from CSI to Velero FSB (Kopia)
Date: 2026-05-10 (revised for dual-cadence architecture)
References: docs/future/restic-fsb-patch.md, docs/operations/why-velero-not-restic.md

This patch flips the **DR-tier Schedule B** from CSI Snapshot path to
Velero's File System Backup (FSB) path with Kopia. Schedule A (operational,
5-min cadence, source-region only) **stays on CSI** — fast restore
remains the operational tier's primary value.

Hybrid pattern outcome:
  - Schedule A: CSI EBS Snapshot, 5-min cadence, source region only
                → Fast operational roll-back; ~25 min RTO via Velero restore
  - Schedule B: FSB Kopia chunks, 4h cadence, source + DR (S3 replicated)
                → Cross-cloud portable, granular file-level restore,
                   archival-tier-cost-friendly

Apply only after Stage 3 conversation establishes the customer's profile
rewards cross-cloud DR portability + granular restore at the DR tier
(see docs/operations/why-velero-not-restic.md trade-off table).

Files modified:
  1. infrastructure/terraform/cluster-controllers.tf  (+10 lines: deployNodeAgent + uploaderType)
  2. helm/aegis-statefulset/templates/velero-schedule-dr.yaml  (~5 lines: switch DR Schedule to FSB)

Files NOT modified:
  - velero-schedule-operational.yaml (stays on CSI, source-region only)
  - velero-storage.tf (existing replicated BSL serves FSB chunks naturally)
  - values.yaml (dual-cadence schema unchanged; FSB respects same cadence settings)

Apply: git apply docs/future/restic-fsb-patch/restic-fsb.patch
If `git apply` rejects on context drift: `git apply --recount`
Verify: terraform validate + helm lint after apply

---

diff --git a/infrastructure/terraform/cluster-controllers.tf b/infrastructure/terraform/cluster-controllers.tf
--- a/infrastructure/terraform/cluster-controllers.tf
+++ b/infrastructure/terraform/cluster-controllers.tf
@@ -123,9 +123,23 @@
   set {
     name  = "serviceAccount.server.annotations.eks\\.amazonaws\\.com/role-arn"
     value = aws_iam_role.velero.arn
   }

+  # AEGIS-PATCH-ANCHOR: restic-fsb
+  # FSB path enabled for DR-tier Schedule B (Kopia uploader, default since
+  # Velero 1.10). Schedule A (operational) continues on CSI. See
+  # docs/future/restic-fsb-patch.md for trade-off rationale.
+  set {
+    name  = "deployNodeAgent"
+    value = "true"
+  }
+
+  set {
+    name  = "configuration.uploaderType"
+    value = "kopia"
+  }
+
   set {
     name  = "configuration.backupStorageLocation[0].name"
     value = "default"
   }
diff --git a/helm/aegis-statefulset/templates/velero-schedule-dr.yaml b/helm/aegis-statefulset/templates/velero-schedule-dr.yaml
--- a/helm/aegis-statefulset/templates/velero-schedule-dr.yaml
+++ b/helm/aegis-statefulset/templates/velero-schedule-dr.yaml
@@ -29,13 +29,17 @@
       - velero
       - karpenter
       - argocd
-    snapshotVolumes: true
-    snapshotMoveData: true  # DR tier: replicate across regions
+    # AEGIS-PATCH-ANCHOR: restic-fsb
+    # FSB path for DR tier — Kopia chunks land in BSL (replicated to
+    # DR region via S3 cross-region replication, NOT via EBS CopySnapshot).
+    # Schedule A (operational) stays on CSI for fast restore.
+    defaultVolumesToFsBackup: true
+    snapshotVolumes: false
+    snapshotMoveData: false  # FSB path: cross-region via S3 replication, not CopySnapshot
     ttl: "{{ .Values.backup.dr.retention_days }}d"
     storageLocation: default  # replicated BSL bucket (velero_bsl)
-    volumeSnapshotLocations:
-      - source-region
-      - dr-region
+    # volumeSnapshotLocations not used in FSB path; cross-region copy
+    # handled by aws_s3_bucket_replication_configuration on velero_bsl.
     hooks:
       resources:
         - name: stateful-fsfreeze
